<body>
    <h1>K12Technology Roadmap</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-K12Modernization">K12 Modernization<=
/h2>
<p>IT Stakeholder Presentation<br>
October 2025</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>College Foundation, Inc.</p></li>
<li>
<p>North Carolina SEAA Programs</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Timeline:</strong> October 15, 2025 - May 1, 2026</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Agenda">Agenda</h2>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Executive Summary</strong> =E2=80=93 Project overview and timeli=
ne</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Modernizaton Scope</p></li>
<li>
<p>Core Capabilities</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Platform Overview</strong> =E2=80=93 Complete system scope</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Tools</p></li>
<li>
<p>Infrastructure</p></li>
<li>
<p>Cross-Cutting Concerns</p></li>
<li>
<p>3rd-Party Integrations</p></li>
<li>
<p>Data Migrations</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Complete Feature Inventory</strong> =E2=80=93 All core capabilit=
ies</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Risk Assessment</strong> =E2=80=93 Critical areas and mitigation=
</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Success Criteria</strong> =E2=80=93 Delivery milestones and qual=
ity metrics</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Next Steps</strong> =E2=80=93 Execution and monitoring</p></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-ExecutiveSummary">Executive Summary</h2>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-CompleteK12ModernizationScope">Complete K12 =
Modernization Scope</h3>
<p><strong>Timeline:</strong> October 15, 2025 - May 1, 2026 (28 weeks)</p>
<p><strong>Platform Serves:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Two scholarship programs (ESA+, Opportunity Scholarship)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Up to 80,000 concurrent users</p></li>
<li>
<p>Four web portals (Household, School, Provider, Admin)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Comprehensive scholarship lifecycle management</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-CoreCapabilitiesRequired">Core Capabilities =
Required</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Household &amp; Student Management (15+ features):</strong> This=
 domain covers the core entry points for end-users. Critical features inclu=
de the <strong>ESA+ and OS application workflows</strong>, <strong>renewal =
processes</strong>, and student profile and account management.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>School Management (20+ features):</strong> This focuses on insti=
tutional requirements, including <strong>school registration and profiles</=
strong>, <strong>annual certification workflows</strong>, and the crucial, =
time-sensitive <strong>semester parent endorsement</strong> process.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Provider Management (12+ features):</strong> This involves manag=
ing service providers (tutors, therapists) who accept ESA+ funds. Key featu=
res include <strong>provider registration and enrollment</strong>, the publ=
ic <strong>provider directory</strong>, and <strong>invoice submission and =
processing</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin Portal Operations (30+ features):</strong> This is the ope=
rational core for SEAA staff, enabling <strong>application processing and r=
eview</strong>, <strong>verification management</strong> (domicile, income,=
 sampling), <strong>award management</strong> (lottery, calculation, lifecy=
cle), and necessary <strong>reporting and analytics</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Payment &amp; Financial Systems (18+ features):</strong> This do=
main handles the disbursement of scholarship funds. Critical requirements i=
nclude <strong>direct payment school processing</strong>, <strong>ESA+ wall=
et and purchasing</strong> (which relies heavily on ClassWallet integration=
), <strong>tax reporting (1099-G)</strong>, <strong>rollover management</st=
rong>, and <strong>minimum spending enforcement</strong> ($1,000 threshold =
for ESA+).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Verification &amp; Compliance (15+ features):</strong> This doma=
in is critical for regulatory adherence and includes eligibility verificati=
on workflows, ongoing compliance monitoring, and <strong>integrations with =
7 state agencies</strong>. The mandatory process of <strong>verification sa=
mpling</strong> (4% of applications) and handling non-cooperation falls her=
e.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Critical Deadline:</strong> <strong>May 1, 2026</strong> - All c=
ore functionality must be production-ready</p>
<hr>
<p>STATUS KEYS:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>NI: NOT IMPLEMENTED</p></li>
<li>
<p>IP: IN PROGRESS</p></li>
<li>
<p>SU: STATUS UNKNOWN</p></li>
<li>
<p>DONE: COMPLETED</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-PlatformArchitecture">Platform Architecture<=
/h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Serverless / Microservices (IP)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Azure Functions, API Management, SQL Database</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Event-driven Processing (IP)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Event Grid, Azure Functions, Azure Logic Apps</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Business Logic Layer (NI)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Rules Engine (IP)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Analysis &amp; Design (NI)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>artifacts (diagrams)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Azure Network</p></li>
<li>
<p>Domain Diagram(s)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Architecture Decision Record (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>SignalR (for Message Center) (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Document Storage (DataLake) (DONE)</p></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>FE: responsive architecture/tools/execution</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Tools">Tools</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Frontend</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>ADA/WCAG compliance (IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Jest (unit testing) (IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>UI Control Suite (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Prettier, Pre-Commit Hooks (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Nx Console/Generators (NI)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Backend</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Rules Engine Framework Selecction (IP)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Infrastructure">Infrastructure</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Network Security (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>CI/CD Piplelines from development to production (IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reliability</p></li>
<li>
<p>Quality</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Testing</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Security</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Package scanning (IP)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Cross-CuttingConcernsRequired">Cross-Cutting=
 Concerns Required</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Observability/Telemetry (IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enrollment Builder (IP)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>UI Admin, Render Engine, Components</p></li>
<li>
<p>Data Mapper</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Entra (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://cfi-nc.atlassian.net/browse/K=
12-4297" rel=3D"nofollow">Communication Center</a> (DONE)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Email</p></li>
<li>
<p>In-application notifications</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Query Builder (Cube Core) (IP)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>reporting</p></li>
<li>
<p>ad-hoc queries</p></li>
<li>
<p>recipient list generation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Task Engine (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Document Storage (DONE)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Versioning</p></li>
<li>
<p>Retention</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>PandaDocs (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Audit Logging (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>PID Generator/Integration (NI)</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-3rd-PartyIntegration(s)">3rd-Party Integrati=
on(s)</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://cfi-nc.atlassian.net/issues/?=
jql=3Dtextfields%20~%20%22CLASSWALLET%2A%22&amp;selectedIssue=3DK12-373&amp=
;wildcardFlag=3Dtrue" rel=3D"nofollow">ClassWallet</a> (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://cfi-nc.atlassian.net/issues/?=
jql=3Dtextfields%20~%20%22RDS%2A%22&amp;selectedIssue=3DK12-2964&amp;wildca=
rdFlag=3Dtrue" rel=3D"nofollow">RDS</a> (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>SparkPost (Email Engine) (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Aperio/CISCO Call Center (Provider Lookup) (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>PandaDocs (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Cube Cloud (API and SDK integration) (IP)</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-DataMigrations">Data Migrations</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Schools (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Providers (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Household and Students (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Operational Data (existing) (NI)</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-K-12SEAAModernizationProject:TechnologyRoadm=
apReport">K-12 SEAA Modernization Project: Technology Roadmap Report</h2>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-1.DefinitionofaTechnologyRoadmap">1. Definit=
ion of a Technology Roadmap</h3>
<p>A Technology Roadmap, in the context of the K-12 SEAA Modernization proj=
ect, is a <strong>strategic, phased delivery plan</strong> covering the ent=
ire scope of work, designed to guide the development teams toward a <strong=
>critical production launch deadline of May 1, 2026</strong>.</p>
<p>Based on the materials, the roadmap functions as the implementation plan=
, detailing the sequential delivery of <strong>110+ distinct features</stro=
ng> across six core functional domains, the integration of <strong>high-ris=
k external systems</strong> (like ClassWallet), and the resolution of criti=
cal architectural and data integrity deficiencies. The roadmap prioritizes =
the delivery of cross-cutting services early to ensure the foundation for <=
strong>security (Entra ID)</strong>, <strong>logic (Rules Engine)</strong>,=
 and <strong>communication (Communication Center)</strong> is stable before=
 executing advanced administrative and financial workflows.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-2.ProjectContextandStateofProject">2. Projec=
t Context and State of Project</h3>
<p>The K-12 SEAA Modernization project has been in development for approxim=
ately one year. The project serves two scholarship programs (ESA+ and Oppor=
tunity Scholarship) and must support up to <strong>80,000 concurrent users<=
/strong> across four web portals (Household, School, Provider, Admin).</p>
<h4 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-CoreFeatures">Core Features</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: <strong>NOT IMPLEMENTED (NI)</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Challenges</strong>: None of the <em>core</em> features are impl=
emented, integrated and/or complete.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Registration and application workflows for ESA+ and Opportunity Scholars=
hip</p></li>
<li>
<p>Renewal processes</p></li>
<li>
<p>School and Provider management portals</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin portal operations for SEAA staff</p></li>
<li>
<p>Payment processing and financial systems</p></li>
<li>
<p>Verification and compliance workflows, including state agency integratio=
ns</p></li>
<li>
<p>Database schema for all domains (modernization)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Resolution</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Implement <code>workflow-centric</code> operations to deliver core featu=
res in a phased manner over the next 7 months.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Start with <strong>foundational</strong> features (i.e., Student, Househ=
old, School, Provider) and <strong>logical sequence(s)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Stop focus on tool-building</p></li>
<li>
<p>Stop focus on "what is easy" (e.g., Provider)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Focus on <code>event-driven</code> <strong>workflows</strong> to decoupl=
e services and improve scalability</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em><strong>REQUIRES</strong></em>: grouping tasks to operational workfl=
ows with application context</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Prioritize high-risk external integrations (ClassWallet, RDS) early in t=
he roadmap</p></li>
<li>
<p>Need application <strong>database</strong> and <strong>resources</strong=
> to enforce relational integrity and domain-driven design</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Implement a <em>coordination</em> of database schemas, changes, and envi=
ronment deployments</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Architecture(Backend)">Architecture (Backend=
)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: <strong>NI / IN PROGRESS (IP)</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Challenges</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Process</strong>: Architecture Design, Analysis, and Decision Re=
cords (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Business Logic Layer (NI)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Workflow</strong> and <strong>Event-driven</strong> Processing (=
IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Strong <strong>Business Logic</strong> with <strong>Rules Engine</strong=
> (IP)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Resolution</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Complete Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) for all major design decis=
ions</p></li>
<li>
<p>Finalize Business Logic Layer design using Rules Engine</p></li>
<li>
<p>Fully implement event-driven architecture with <code>Workflow-centric</c=
ode> operations and <strong>Task</strong> Engine</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em><strong>REQUIRES</strong></em>: grouping tasks to <strong>operationa=
l workflows</strong> with application context</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Architecture(Frontend)">Architecture (Fronte=
nd)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: <strong>New</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Challenges</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>(4) autonomous teams working in silos without architectural governance</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Consistent components communication (i.e., API, responses ) patterns not=
 established</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enterprise cross-cutting concerns (i.e., logging, error handling, teleme=
try) not implemented/standardized</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Resolution</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>(1) Frontend Architect to coordinate implementation of patterns, compone=
nts, and shared libraries</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Adding core cross-cutting concerns (i.e., logging, error handling, and c=
onfiguration)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Document and socialize standards for API contracts, responses, and error=
 handling</p></li>
<li>
<p>Establish architectural governance process for all teams to follow</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Implement shared libraries for cross-cutting concerns and utilities</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>shared models and DTO library projects</p></li>
<li>
<p>shared layout and styles/assets library projects</p></li>
<li>
<p>Data access layer with repository pattern (i.e., Http Service)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-Cross-CuttingServices">Cross-Cutting Service=
s</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: <strong>DONE / IP</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Details</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Microsoft Entra (Security) (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Communication Center (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>SignalR (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>PandaDocs (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Document Storage (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Rules Engine (IP)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Observability/Telemetry (IP).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Resolution</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Complete implementation and integration of Rules Engine with business lo=
gic</p></li>
<li>
<p>Finalize Observability/Telemetry for end-to-end monitoring and diagnosti=
cs</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>AppInsights, Log Analytics, Distributed Tracing</p></li>
<li>
<p>by Application (i.e., frontend and backend), environment</p></li>
<li>
<p>monitoring dashboards and alerts (thresholds)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"K12TechnologyRoadmap-3rd-PartyIntegrations">3rd-Party Integration=
s</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Status</strong>: <strong>NI / DONE / IP</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Details</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>SparkPost (Email Engine) (DONE)</p></li>
<li>
